# Phase K4 (docs/nvidia-proprietary.md), only on the entry with androidboot.android_pc.gpu=nvidia.
#
# drm_hwcomposer (the entry's composer APEX) drives nvidia-drm (modeset=1): atomic commits,
# the monitor's preferred mode, hotplug through DRM uevents, vsync from nvidia-drm's vblank
# events, present fences from OUT_FENCE_PTR, and the client target's acquire fence (a Venus
# sync_file from the vtest server, or -1) as the plane's IN_FENCE_FD, which nvidia-drm waits
# for before the flip. Overlay planes stay off as on the nouveau entries
# (ro.vendor.hwc.use_overlay_planes=0, set by K1's block in init.pc.rc): SurfaceFlinger
# composes every layer (ANGLE on Venus, i.e. NVIDIA's Vulkan in the sidecar) into its client
# target, and only that buffer is scanned out; pcnvdisplay makes sure its modifier is one the
# primary plane takes.
#
# Runs before class hal (composer, allocator) starts at boot. Waits up to 30 s for nvidia-drm's
# card when an NVIDIA GPU is on the PCI bus, returns at once otherwise (QEMU).
on post-fs-data && property:ro.boot.android_pc.gpu=nvidia
    exec u:r:su:s0 root graphics -- /vendor/bin/pcnvdisplay
